---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import Row from '../../components/Row.astro';
import { RELEASE, TRIAL } from '../../data/site';

// Install and first launch, in the app's own words (the setup screens in
// crates/vault-tauri/dist/app.js; the /docs/ hub's Getting started keeps a
// short version that links here).
const win = RELEASE.windows;
const mac = RELEASE.mac;
const OUTLINE = [
  { id: 'before', title: 'Before you start' },
  { id: 'install', title: 'Install' },
  { id: 'set-up', title: 'Set up' },
  { id: 'next', title: 'What to do next' },
];
---
<Guide
  path="/docs/getting-started/"
  lede={`Download Zaaheen for Windows or Mac and install it, then choose Begin set up. Setting up takes about three minutes: you sign in from the app, which starts your ${TRIAL.days}-day free trial (no card needed), choose where your memories live, and connect your first AI app.`}
  outline={OUTLINE}
>
  <section class="docs-section">
    <Row level={2} id="before" title="Before you start" where="Windows or Mac">
      {!RELEASE.available && <p><strong>Zaaheen for Windows and Mac is coming soon.</strong> These
         steps are how it works once you can download it.</p>}
      <p>Zaaheen {RELEASE.version} is a {RELEASE.stage.toLowerCase()} for {win.arch} Windows, tested
         on {win.tested}, and for Macs with an Apple chip, M1 or newer, tested on {mac.tested}. It is
         not available for Linux or phones yet.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="install" title="Install" where="Windows or Mac">
      <p><strong>On Windows,</strong> open the installer you downloaded. You may see up to three
         questions on the way, and each is expected:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Microsoft Edge says the file "isn't commonly downloaded".</strong> The installer is
            new, so Edge has not seen it often. Choose the three dots next to the download, then
            <em>Keep</em>, <em>Show more</em> and <em>Keep anyway</em>. Chrome does not ask.</li>
        <li><strong>Windows says the publisher is unknown.</strong> Zaaheen is in beta, and the
            installer is not code-signed yet; signing comes later. Choose
            <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run anyway</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Windows asks for administrator permission.</strong> Zaaheen installs for everyone
            on the computer, so Windows asks once. It does not need administrator rights to run
            afterwards.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>On a Mac,</strong> open the disk image you downloaded, drag Zaaheen into the
         Applications folder, then open Zaaheen from Applications. Zaaheen only runs from there.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your Mac asks whether to open an app downloaded from the internet.</strong> It
            names the developer. The Mac app is signed and checked by Apple. Choose
            <em>Open</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Your Mac may ask whether Zaaheen can use your keychain.</strong> That is where
            the key to your memories is kept. Choose <em>Always Allow</em>.</li>
      </ul>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="set-up" title="Set up" where="Begin set up">
      <p>Open Zaaheen and choose <em>Begin set up</em>. It walks you through five steps:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Your account.</strong> Choose <em>Create an account</em> or <em>Sign in</em>. This
            opens your web browser. Your {TRIAL.days}-day free trial starts the first time you sign
            in from the Zaaheen app, and no card is needed. Signing in never shares your memories
            with us.</li>
        <li><strong>Where to keep your memories.</strong> The usual place suits most people. You can
            change it later from Settings with <em>Move my memories…</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Your first AI app.</strong> Pick the app you use and follow the steps, or choose
            <em>I'll connect one later</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Your first memory.</strong> Tell Zaaheen something your AI apps should know about
            you, then choose <em>Keep this memory</em>, or <em>Skip for now</em>.</li>
        <li><strong>Tidying up.</strong> Zaaheen tidies your memory on its own each night unless you
            choose <em>Not now</em>, then <em>Finish setup</em>.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>The first time, Zaaheen also downloads what it needs to search your memories. It does this
         in the background, and you can use Zaaheen while it finishes.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row level={2} id="next" title="What to do next" where="Agents">
      <p>Connect the AI apps you use, each once, from the <em>Agents</em> tab:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/docs/connect-claude/">Connect Claude Desktop</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/connect-claude-code/">Connect Claude Code</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/connect-cursor/">Connect Cursor</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/connect-chatgpt/">Connect ChatGPT</a></li>
        <li><a href="/docs/connect-other-apps/">Connect other AI apps</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>If something doesn't work as described, see <a href="/docs/troubleshooting/">Fixing common
         problems</a>.</p>
    </Row>
  </section>
</Guide>
